msgid "Refresh: look for gamepads and joysticks again. This also happens by itself a moment after a pad is plugged in or out while this window is open."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2766
msgid "How fast a Turbo button fires while it is held (set for A, B, C, X, Y or Z with a right-click). Slower presses it 7.5 times a second, Slow 10, Medium 15 (the default), Fast 22.5 and Faster 30 (the most a game can see at 60 frames a second)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2767
msgid "Choose This Tab (the one that is showing) or All Tabs: they go back to their defaults (OK keeps the change)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2768
msgid "Go through the pad buttons one after another, pressing a key or button for each."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2769
msgid "Try your keys: while ticked, the keyboard no longer moves around or presses buttons in this window, so you can press Enter, Tab, Esc and the arrows and see the pad spots light."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2770
msgid "Choose which gamepad button runs each shortcut: fast forward, rewind, save and load state, previous and next slot."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2771
msgid "What is plugged into the console's first controller port: a pad, mouse, light gun, Team Player and so on. Netplay needs a plain Control Pad on both ports."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2772
msgid "Allows Left and Right, or Up and Down, to be held at the same time. A real pad cannot do it, so only one of the two reaches the game; a few games and glitch tricks need both."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2773
msgid "What is plugged into the console's second controller port: a pad, mouse, light gun, Team Player and so on. Netplay needs a plain Control Pad on both ports."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2774
msgid "A saved set of controls: both players' keys and buttons, pad types, deadzones, turbo buttons and rate, and the combos (not the ports). Pick a saved profile from the list, or type a name for a new one. Restore Defaults puts the program's own controls back."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2775
msgid "Load the profile named in the box into this window (OK keeps it). Grayed when no profile is saved."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2776
msgid "Make a new profile from this window's controls, under the name typed in the box."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2777
msgid "Save this window's controls into the loaded profile. If you typed another name in the box, it renames the loaded profile to it (it asks)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2778
msgid "Delete the profile named in the box (it asks first)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2779
msgid "A short explanation of how to make a combo, with an example."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2780
msgid "Trigger:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2780
msgid "The key or gamepad button that sets the combo off. Click here, then press it (Esc or a right click cancels). A letter or digit, F1-F12, Num0-Num9, Space, an arrow key or an XInput pad button can be used."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2781
msgid "Hold:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2781
msgid "Click it after an action button to make that action Held: it stays down by itself once the trigger has been pressed, for the time you choose in the menu (or until you press that button yourself). Shown as Down(Hold 1.0s)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2782
msgid "Pause:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2782
msgid "Click it between two action buttons to wait before the next action starts, for the time you choose in the menu. Shown as Pause 0.5s. Without one, the action after a Held one starts 70 ms later (Down, then A)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2783
msgid "Take the last action (and the pause before it) off the end of the combo."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2784
msgid "Delete the combo selected in the list (the row being worked on)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2785
msgid "Saved Combos:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2785
msgid "The combos set up so far: the row number, the trigger and the actions. Pick one to add to it or to change it."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2786
msgid "Save the controls of both players."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2787
msgid "Close without saving (the port devices go back as they were)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2807
msgid "Turbo for button %s: while it is held, the button fires on and off repeatedly (Turbo Rate sets how fast)."
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2809
msgid "Turbo:"
msgstr ""

#: dialogs.c:2817
msgid "%s: adds it to the combo on the trigger above (the combo is made on the first click). Then Hold and Pause shape how it is pressed."
msgstr ""

